TI  - Research progress of indocyanine green fluorescence technology in gynecological 
      applications.
PG  - 936-942
LID - 10.1002/ijgo.15249 [doi]
AB  - Indocyanine green is a near-infrared fluorescent dye which is widely used in 
      various fields of surgery and gynecology. It is currently mainly used to detect 
      various malignant tumors, sentinel lymph nodes, endometriosis lesions, ureter or 
      intestinal occlusion, vaginal perfusion, uterine arterial blood perfusion, pelvic 
      nerve, uterine niche, lymphatic edema, metastatic lesion shadow, and so on, 
      providing new methods for decision-making during surgery. This article elaborates 
      the application progress of indocyanine green fluorescence technology in 
      gynecology.
