TI  - Isthmocele-a neglected cause of secondary infertility and implantation failure: A 
      case report.
PG  - e05853
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.5853 [doi]
LID - e05853
AB  - Isthmocele is myometrial scar tissue that develops after cesarean section 
      delivery. In this case, other more prevalent pathologies delayed isthmocele 
      diagnosis as the main cause of the patient's symptoms. Considering isthmocele is 
      a fluid-filled pouch-like defect associated with infection caused by stagnant 
      menstrual blood, its immunological aspects lead to implantation failure.
