AB  - Isthmocele is a growing pathology due to the increase in the number of cesarean 
      deliveries. Pelvic pain and abnormal uterine bleeding are common complaints in 
      our clinical practice, and isthmocele should be included in the differential 
      diagnosis, especially in women who underwent previous cesarean sections.
