TI  - Laparoscopic management of cesarean scar pregnancy: Report of two cases with 
      video-presentation of different operative techniques and literature review.
PG  - 102066
LID - S2468-7847(21)00008-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jogoh.2021.102066 [doi]
AB  - Cesarean scar pregnancy (CSP) is a rare form of ectopic pregnancy. We present two 
      different techniques of laparoscopic management of CSP, with the concomitant 
      repair of the coexisting uterine isthmocele. The first case is a combination of 
      diagnostic hysteroscopy and laparoscopic extraction of conception products, and 
      the second technique is a combination of laparoscopy and guided Dilation & 
      Curettage. We also conducted a thorough review of the literature to present all 
      cases of laparoscopic treatment of CSP, focusing on the surgical technique, the 
      operation outcome, and the future pregnancies. Laparoscopy is a potential 
      effective treatment of CSP.
